b_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Found in v4.5.1.stable.official [f62fdbde1]\n- Not reproducible in v4.3.stable.official [77dcf97d8] (and 4.1 and 4.2.2)\n- Reproducible in v4.4.stable.official [4c311cbee]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.1.stable - Windows 11 (build 26100) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce GTX 950 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.8129) - AMD Ryzen 9 5900XT 16-Core Processor (32 threads) - 31.91 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nSelecting a new tile in the TileSet editor's \"select\" tab while still have an un-confirmed change on the currently selected tile results in the change being applied to the second tile instead of the first.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create a TileSet with multiple tiles.\n2. Go to the select tab on the TileSet editor and click on a tile.\n3. Change a property of the currently selected tile: it has to be one with a spinbox. **Don't press enter to confirm the change!** (I used y-sort origin)\n4. Click on a different tile.\nThe change should only be applied to the tiled you clicked on second, instead of the first one.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[tileset_test.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/24280872/tileset_test.zip)\n\nThis project only has a TileSet that's set up for the reproduction steps.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114275/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114275/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}